{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg1NvnaRRWhLY92oN3BGQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I give up.\n\nThe statement is Putnam 2015 A6, and I don't have a proof I can formalize within these constraints. The argument I see is the following. Since AM = MB, A preserves im M and B preserves ker M. Comparing charpolys on those invariant subspaces gives equal charpolys for the induced quotient maps. Then det(A − MX) = det[[A, M],[X, I]] = det[[B, X],[M, I]] = det(B − XM) via Schur complements. Making this work in Lean needs basis changes to block-triangular form, charpoly multiplicativity over invariant subspaces, and the block-determinant identities. I did not get that to compile, and I did not check the Mathlib lemma names. The file `/work/putnam_2015_a6.lean` is unchanged and still contains the `sorry`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":424,"cache_read_input_tokens":3606,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":424,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2aaf181-8926-492f-825a-e83addb68db3","uuid":"12d6f7eb-4778-4b8b-bdf9-0f83edb3934b","timestamp":"2026-10-14T02:57:45.978Z","request_id":"req_011Cg1NvnFbEku9EdsbY7Lvc"}
